why Every Horde quest of Razorfen Kraul in one run, lead-ins included.

# Razorfen Kraul's Horde quests in one guide: the pick-ups in Thunder Bluff,
# the Undercity and Ratchet (for Warriors and Shamans their class chains too),
# one run, then the hand-ins. Steps already done are passed over, so the guide
# picks up wherever the chain stands.
#
# The quests: Auld Stonespire's 1102 A Vengeful Fate (Charlga's heart); Master
# Apothecary Faranell's 1109 Going, Going, Guano!; Mebok Mizzyrix's 1221
# Blueleaf Tubers (with the crate, manual and command stick by him); inside,
# Charlga's Small Scroll (item 17008) starts 6522 An Unholy Alliance (for
# Varimathras), and Willix the Importer gives 1144 (an escort). Warriors: Torm
# Ragetotem's 1823 -> Ruga Ragetotem's 1824 Trial at the Field of Giants ->
# 1825 -> Thun'grim Firegaze's 1838 Brutal Armor (Smoky Iron Ingots in
# Stonetalon, Powdered Azurite in Hillsbrad, Iron Bars, Roogug's Vial of
# Phlogiston). Shamans: Xanis Flameweaver's 1532 Call of Air -> Prate
# Cloudseer's 79360 Elemental Aid (Charlga's Tattered Note, for Rau
# Cliffrunner).
#
# Follow-ups: Thun'grim Firegaze's 1848 Brutal Hauberk (Warriors) and Rau
# Cliffrunner's 79364 Eyes on the Sky (Shamans, to Prate Cloudseer).
#
# Left out: 1113 Hearts of Zeal, Faranell's follow-up (Scarlet Monastery), and
# 6521 An Unholy Alliance, Varimathras' (Razorfen Downs): they are in those
# dungeons' guides. 1531 and 96136 Call of Air are the same Shaman lead-in from
# Orgrimmar and (for Skyborne) Mulgore.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses or Willix inside, so their
# goals stand at the door (@42.9,90.2, The Barrens) with `group 5`. The steps
# follow a run of my own: Death Speaker Jargba, Aggem Thorncurse, Overlord
# Ramtusk, Roogug, the guano from the bats, Agathelos, Charlga Razorflank, then
# Willix's escort. Every quest goal is counted by the quest log, so a group
# that takes them in another order still gets each step ticked.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon. The guano drops from the Kraul Bats and the
#   Blind Hunter.
# - The door: QuestieDB's list of Forever's dungeons, as Polestar's Codex holds it
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - A run of my own on 2026-11-11 (Horde, five players, level 31), recorded
#   with Polestar's recorder and shared with Polestar Client: the bosses in the
#   order above, the guano after Roogug, Charlga's heart and the Small Scroll,
#   Willix taken and escorted after Charlga, the tubers along the way.
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   29 to 38). Several of its quests need level 30, so the guide starts there.

